*20
/         QUESTIONS:
/1.  BILL MCGOWAN WAS FAMOUS IN
/(A) TENNIS
/(B) BASKETBALL
/(C) BASEBALL
/(D) FOOTBALL
	C
/2.  AT THE TIME THE ARTICLE WAS WRITTEN, MCGOWAN WAS
/(A) RETIRED
/(B) WORKING IN CONNECTION WITH A WORLD SERIES GAME
/(C) JUST ELECTED AN OFFICIAL
/(D) DECEASED
	D
/3.  THE PROUDEST MOMENT OF HIS LIFE WAS WHEN THE AMERICAN
/LEAGUE NAMED HIM
/(A) CAPTAIN
/(B) COACH
/(C) DIRECTOR
/(D) UMPIRE-IN-CHIEF
	D
/4.  BILL WAS
/(A) A PESSIMIST
/(B) OPTIMIST
/(C) ENTHUSIAST
/(D) CHRONIC COMPLAINER
	C
/5. BILL EVEN PRACTICED
/(A) IN HIS KITCHEN
/(B) WHILE TRAVELING ON THE TRAIN
/(C) BEFORE THE MIRROR IN HIS HOTEL ROOM
/(D) IN HIS LOCKER ROOM
	C
/6.  IT WAS INDICATED THAT MCGOWAN"S SALARY WAS
/(A) HIGH
/(B) EXORBITANT
/(C) MODEST
/(D) INCREASED THREEFOLD DURING HIS LAST TEN YEARS OF WORK
	C
/7.  BILL PICKED A MAN FROM THE LOBBY TO ENTERTAIN,
/THINKING THAT THIS MAN WAS A GOOD PROSPECT FOR
/(A) HELPING BILL GET A SALARY RAISE
/(B) HELPING HIM GET A PROMOTION
/(C) LETTING HIM HAVE CLOTHES AT WHOLESALE PRICES OR FREE
/(D) TEACHING HIM A NEW TRICK IN BASEBALL
	C
/8. THE ARTICLE MENTIONED THAT MCGOWAN WAS SUSPENDED
/(A) ONCE
/(B) TWICE
/(C) MANY TIMES
/(D) NEVER
	B
/9.  ONE OF BILL"S SUSPENSIONS RESULTED FROM
/(A) UNFAIR PLAY
/(B) ILL HEALTH
/(C) A HOT EXCHANGE OF WORDS WITH THE PRESS
/(D) A QUARREL WITH THE PRESIDENT OF THE AMERICAN LEAGUE
	C
/10.  BALLPLAYERS REGARDED BILL WITH
/(A) JEALOUSY
/(B) ANIMOSITY
/(C) PITY
/(D) AFFECTION
	D
